        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            At the value end the machines are more similar than the badges suggest, so
            <strong class="text-white">buy the listing rather than the brand</strong>. A pad that cut
            the console and the incline is a sound buy; one that cut the deck, the minimum speed or
            the frame is not, at any price.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Verify the minimum speed first, use the returns window as the real test it is, and
            <a href="/how-often-to-lubricate-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubricate from month one</a>
            — a budget motor has the least headroom in the category, so it needs the routine most.
